  <document-link format="APPLICATION/HTTP" url="https://www.chsalliance.org/get-support/training/investigator-qualification-training-scheme/">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investigator Qualification Training Scheme (IQTS)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">IQTS uses a tiered approach to training that aims to build and enhance investigation competencies progressively, and which is based on professionally developed standards of investigating allegations of sexual misconduct.

The scheme supports career progression through ongoing training and support in four tiers.</narrative>
   </description>
   <category code="A08"></category>
   <language code="EN"></language>
   <document-date iso-date="2023-12-31"></document-date>
  </document-link>
  <document-link format="APPLICATION/PDF" url="https://d1h79zlghft2zs.cloudfront.net/uploads/2022/04/IQTS_SEAH_Investigation_Guide.pdf">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Harassment (SEAH) Investigation Guide</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Harassment (SEAH) Investigation Guide: Recommended Practice for the Humanitarian and Development Sector  is the foundation of the SEAH Investigator Qualification Training Scheme (IQTS).

The guide explains the structured investigation processes necessary to professionally investigate Sexual Exploitation, Abuse and Harassment (SEAH) incidents in the humanitarian and development sector. It provides best practice guidance, tools, and steps for conducting survivor-centered SEAH investigations.

The IQTS scheme is a collaborative effort between CHS Alliance, Humentum and the UK Government&#x2019;s Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office to develop a training scheme to improve the quality of safeguarding investigations carried out by NGOs and international bodies.</narrative>
   </description>
   <category code="A08"></category>
   <language code="EN"></language>
   <document-date iso-date="2022-03-31"></document-date>
